</math> members has <math alttext="11"><mn>11</mn>
</math> members who play saxophone. If one band member is selected at random, what is the probability of selecting a band member who plays saxophone?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"d2245596-14c8-4f5a-97ce-f20d012f40fe","content":"<p><math alttext=\"one forty fifth\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>45</mn></mfrac></math></p>"},{"id":"6e8e4f33-55f5-4a26-b491-f6d88fff5eef","content":"<p><math alttext=\"StartFraction 11 Over 45 EndFraction\"><mfrac><mn>11</mn><mn>45</mn></mfrac></math></p>"},{"id":"2464afe7-c779-468c-a296-53c06f7f470d","content":"<p><math alttext=\"StartFraction 34 Over 45 EndFraction\"><mfrac><mn>34</mn><mn>45</mn></mfrac></math></p>"},{"id":"d76b7dc4-c30e-4b41-bced-fb7b8df67830","content":"<p><math alttext=\"StartFraction 45 Over 45 EndFraction\"><mfrac><mn>45</mn><mn>45</mn></mfrac></math></p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["B"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["6e8e4f33-55f5-4a26-b491-f6d88fff5eef"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p style="text-align: left;">Choice B is correct. The probability of an event occurring is the ratio of the number of favorable outcomes to the total number of possible outcomes. It&rsquo;s given that there are <math alttext="45"><mn>45</mn>
</math> band members, which is the total number of possible outcomes. It's also given that there are <math alttext="11"><mn>11</mn>
</math> band members who play saxophone. Therefore, the number of favorable outcomes is <math alttext="11"><mn>11</mn>
</math>. Thus, the probability of selecting a band member who plays saxophone is <math alttext="StartFraction 11 Over 45 EndFraction"><mfrac><mn>11</mn><mn>45</mn></mfrac></math>.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice A is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice C is incorrect. This is the probability of selecting a band member who does not play saxophone.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice D is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>$SATQ$, false, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$manifold$SATQ$, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"79201024","external_id":"ab06bbba-a7a0-4fff-8ab6-c9cf37ff575c","disclosed_item_id":null,"source":"qbank","vaultid":"cf4ca0ca-0706-4482-a6ad-67831f7df3a3","uId":"503c3b16-c0f5-4680-b043-30ac59a11b9a","program":"SAT","test_type":2,"test_type_desc":"Math","primary_class_cd":"Q","domain":"Problem-Solving and Data Analysis","skill_cd":"Q.E.","skill_desc":"Probability and conditional probability","difficulty":"E","score_band_range_cd":1,"type":"mcq","stimulus":null,"stem":"<p>A band with <math alttext=\"45\"><mn>45</mn>\n</math> members has <math alttext=\"11\"><mn>11</mn>\n</math> members who play saxophone. If one band member is selected at random, what is the probability of selecting a band member who plays saxophone?</p>","answerOptions":[{"id":"d2245596-14c8-4f5a-97ce-f20d012f40fe","content":"<p><math alttext=\"one forty fifth\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>45</mn></mfrac></math></p>"},{"id":"6e8e4f33-55f5-4a26-b491-f6d88fff5eef","content":"<p><math alttext=\"StartFraction 11 Over 45 EndFraction\"><mfrac><mn>11</mn><mn>45</mn></mfrac></math></p>"},{"id":"2464afe7-c779-468c-a296-53c06f7f470d","content":"<p><math alttext=\"StartFraction 34 Over 45 EndFraction\"><mfrac><mn>34</mn><mn>45</mn></mfrac></math></p>"},{"id":"d76b7dc4-c30e-4b41-bced-fb7b8df67830","content":"<p><math alttext=\"StartFraction 45 Over 45 EndFraction\"><mfrac><mn>45</mn><mn>45</mn></mfrac></math></p>"}],"keys":["6e8e4f33-55f5-4a26-b491-f6d88fff5eef"],"correct_answer":["B"],"rationale":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice B is correct. The probability of an event occurring is the ratio of the number of favorable outcomes to the total number of possible outcomes. It&rsquo;s given that there are <math alttext=\"45\"><mn>45</mn>\n</math> band members, which is the total number of possible outcomes. It