<p>Which of the following is the largest population to which the results of the study can be generalized?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"97c31ab4-cb43-4ac4-9712-b7391f3fa38b","content":"<p>All trivia teams in the tournament that scored <math alttext=\"14\"><mn>14</mn>\n</math> or more points in the round</p>"},{"id":"18100a68-a590-4c06-954a-65eb61ad7049","content":"<p>The <math alttext=\"55\"><mn>55</mn>\n</math> trivia teams in the sample</p>"},{"id":"c865bbc0-a1c8-4045-aeab-e79e04f750b9","content":"<p>The <math alttext=\"40\"><mn>40</mn>\n</math> trivia teams in the sample that practiced for at least <math alttext=\"3\"><mn>3</mn>\n</math> hours per week</p>"},{"id":"512026e5-90cc-4a31-a065-29676bf9e303","content":"<p>All trivia teams in the tournament</p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["D"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["512026e5-90cc-4a31-a065-29676bf9e303"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p style="text-align: left;">Choice D is correct. It's given that the organizer selected <math alttext="55"><mn>55</mn>
</math> teams at random from all trivia teams in the tournament. A table is also given displaying the information for the <math alttext="40"><mn>40</mn>
</math> teams in the sample that practiced for at least <math alttext="3"><mn>3</mn>
</math> hours per week. Selecting a sample of a reasonable size at random to use for a survey allows the results from that survey to be applied to the population from which the sample was selected, but not beyond this population. Thus, only the sampling method information is necessary to determine the largest population to which the results of the study can be generalized. Since the organizer selected the sample at random from all trivia teams in the tournament, the largest population to which the results of the study can be generalized is all trivia teams in the tournament.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice A is incorrect. The sample was selected at random from all trivia teams in the tournament, not just from the teams that scored an average of <math alttext="14"><mn>14</mn>
</math> or more points per round.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice B is incorrect. If a study uses a sample selected at random from a population, the results of the study can be generalized to the population, not just the sample.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice C is incorrect. If a study uses a sample selected at random from a population, the results of the study can be generalized to the population, not just a subset of the sample.</p>$SATQ$, false, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$manifold$SATQ$, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"7d68096f","external_id":"86e6dfb4-d2c8-45de-afe3-b133ed0d88a5","disclosed_item_id":null,"source":"qbank","vaultid":"438d2407-07b6-47b8-a393-17d52aedc2a6","uId":"72ae19c1-ca3a-42f7-8174-68187e2fb57b","program":"SAT","test_type":2,"test_type_desc":"Math","primary_class_cd":"Q","domain":"Problem-Solving and Data Analysis","skill_cd":"Q.G.","skill_desc":"Evaluating statistical claims: Observational studies and experiments ","difficulty":"H","score_band_range_cd":7,"type":"mcq","stimulus":null,"stem":"<p>A trivia tournament organizer wanted to study the relationship between the number of points a team scores in a trivia round and the number of hours that a team practices each week. For the study, the organizer selected <math alttext=\"55\"><mn>55</mn>\n</math> teams at random from all trivia teams in a certain tournament. The table displays the information for the <math alttext=\"40\"><mn>40</mn>\n</math> teams in the sample that practiced for at least <math alttext=\"3\"><mn>3</mn>\n</math> hours per week.</p>\n<figure class=\"table\"><table border=\"1\">\n<thead>\n<tr style=\"height: 22.3906px;\">\n<th style=\"text-align: center; height: 22.3906px; width: 25.0771%;\" rowspan=\"2\" scope=\"colgroup\">Hours practiced</th>\n<th style=\"width: 75.2312%; text-align: center; height: 22.3906px;\" colspan=\"3\" scope=\"colgroup\">Number of points per round</th>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 44.7812px;\">\n<th style=\"width: 25.0771%; text-align: center; height: 44.7812px;\" scope=\"col\">6 to 13 points</th>\n<th style=\"width: 25.0771%; text-align: center; height: 44.7812px;\" scope=\"col\">14 or more points</th>\n<th style=\"width: 25.0771%; text-align: center; heigh