          <p class="stem_paragraph ">The table above shows the amount of protein in two foods and the cost of each food. Based on the table, what is the ratio of the cost per gram of protein in a large egg to the cost per gram of protein in a cup of&nbsp;milk?</p></div>
$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"a","content":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \">1 : 2</p>\n"},{"id":"b","content":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \">2 : 3</p>\n"},{"id":"c","content":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \">3 : 4</p>\n"},{"id":"d","content":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \">2 : 1</p>\n"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["D"]$SATQ$::jsonb, NULL, $SATQ$<p>Choice D is correct. The cost per gram of protein in 1 large egg is $0.36 &divide; 6 = $0.06. The cost per gram of protein in 1 cup of milk is $0.24 &divide; 8 = $0.03. It follows that the ratio of the cost per gram of protein in a large egg to the cost per gram of protein in a cup of milk is&nbsp;0.06:0.03, which can be rewritten as 2:1.<p>Choice A is incorrect and may result from finding the ratio of the cost per gram of protein in a cup of milk to the cost per gram of protein in a large egg (the reciprocal of the ratio specified in the question). Choices B and C are incorrect and may result from incorrectly calculating the unit rates or from errors made when simplifying the ratio.</p></p>
$SATQ$, false, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$Multiple Choice$SATQ$, $SATQ$Math$SATQ$, $SATQ${"questionId":"7e6c745f","external_id":null,"disclosed_item_id":"14884-DC","source":"disclosed","program":"SAT","test_type":2,"test_type_desc":"Math","primary_class_cd":"Q","domain":"Problem-Solving and Data Analysis","skill_cd":"Q.A.","skill_desc":"Ratios, rates, proportional relationships, and units","difficulty":"M","score_band_range_cd":5,"type":"mcq","stimulus":null,"stem":"<div class=\"table_wrapper \">\n            <table class=\"table\">\n              <tbody>\n                <tr>\n                  <td>\n                    <div class=\"tcp-a653250b-9ada-459e-a4d6-1c3c5f5f5740\">\n                      <table class=\"table_WithBorder tcp-bae8268e-ac23-4700-bdf3-f03c96ba18bd\">\n                        <tbody>\n                          <tr>\n                            <td class=\"tcp-15a08c4c-7067-4d81-bcc4-9c330ff02949\">Food</td>\n                            <td class=\"tcp-19ff16e8-e784-4d6b-8693-2e1221445231\">Protein&nbsp;</td>\n                            <td class=\"tcp-3b9dfc4d-a5ba-4889-8993-c88be87e0f90\">Cost</td>\n                          </tr>\n                          <tr>\n                            <td class=\"tcp-cca517e2-df6f-4aff-b5a2-0d56da8f2cf7\">1 large egg</td>\n                            <td class=\"tcp-9d7ff16a-64b5-4a37-a2c2-65bc1f3605f6\">6 grams</td>\n                            <td class=\"tcp-61f11c1c-c32a-4ad3-895e-08bd138e0de3\">$0.36</td>\n                          </tr>\n                          <tr>\n                            <td class=\"tcp-7c3b063b-fe28-4c4d-91e5-8aac8e199b54\">1 cup of milk</td>\n                            <td class=\"tcp-00fe9016-5ef3-42a8-977f-482083e9a4e4\">8 grams</td>\n                            <td class=\"tcp-123badb1-e35d-4cb0-b16b-a8bfbbf7f31d\">$0.24</td>\n                          </tr>\n                        </tbody>\n                      </table>\n                    </div>\n                  </td>\n                </tr>\n              </tbody>\n            </table>\n          <p class=\"stem_paragraph \">The table above shows the amount of protein in two foods and the cost of each food. Based on the table, what is the ratio of the cost per gram of protein in a large egg to the cost per gram of protein in a cup of&nbsp;milk?</p></div>\n","answerOptions":[{"id":"a","content":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \">1 : 2</p>\n"},{"id":"b","content":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \">2 : 3</p>\n"},{"id":"c","content":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \">3 : 4</p>\n"},{"id":"d","content":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \">2 : 1</p>\n"}],"keys":null,"correct_answer":["D"],"rationale":"<p>Choice D is correct. The cost per gram of protein in 1 large egg is $0.36 &divide; 6 = $0.06. The cost per gram of protein in 1 cup of milk is $0.24 &divide; 8 = $0.03. It follows that the ratio of the cost per gram of protein in a large egg to the cost per gram of protein in a cup of milk is&nbsp;0.06:0.03, which can be rewritten as 2:1.<p>Choice A is incorrect and may result from finding the ratio of the cost per gram of protein in a cup of milk to the cost per gram of protein in a large egg (the reciprocal of the ratio specified in the question). Choices B and C are incorrect and may result from incorrectly calculating the unit rates or from errors made when simplifying the ratio.</p></p>\n","answer_style":"Multiple Choice","section":"Math","image_count":0,"raw_list":{"updateDate":1691007959639,"pPcc":"SAT#Q","questionId":"7e6c745f","skill_cd":"Q.A.","score_band_range_cd":5,"skill_desc":"Ratios, rates, proportional relationships, and units","createDate":1691007959639,"program":"SAT","primary_class_cd_desc":"Problem-Solving and Data Analysis","ibn":"14884-DC","external_id":null,"primary_class_cd":"Q","uId":"7b56f747-acfa-4612-8d09-3edfcf74030f","difficulty":"M"},"raw_detail":{"item_id":"14884-DC","section":"Math","prompt":"<div class=\"table_wrapper \">\n            <table class=\"table\">\n              <tbody>\n                <tr>\n                  <td>\n                    <div class=\"tcp-a653250b-9ada-459e-a4d6-1c3c5f5f5740\">\n                      <table class=\"table_WithBorder tcp-bae8268e-ac23-4700-bdf3-f03c96ba18bd\">\n                        <tbody>\n                          <tr>\n                            <td class=\"tcp-15a08c4c-7067-4d81-bcc4-9c330ff02949\">Food</td>\n                            <td class=\"tcp-19ff16e8-e784-4d6b-8693-2e1221445231\">Protein&nbsp;</td>\n                            <td class=\"tcp-3b9dfc4d-a5ba-4889-8993-c88be87e0f90\">Cost</td>\n                          </tr>\n                          <tr>\n                            <td class=\"tcp-cca517e2-df6f-4aff-b5a2-0d56da8f2cf7\">1 large egg</td>\n                            <td class=\"tcp-9d7ff16a-64b5-4a37-a2c2-65bc1f3605f6\">6 grams</td>\n                            <td class=\"tcp-61f11c1c-c32a-4ad3-895e-08bd138e0de3\">$0.36</td>\n                          </tr>\n                          <tr>\n                            <td class=\"tcp-7c3b063b-fe28-4c4d-91e5-8aac8e199b54\">1 cup of milk</td>\n                            <td class=\"tcp-00fe9016-5ef3-42a8-977f-482083e9a4e4\">8 grams</td>\n                            <td class=\"tcp-123badb1-e35d-4cb0-b16b-a8bfbbf7f31d\">$0.24</td>\n                          </tr>\n                        </tbody>\n                      </table>\n                    </div>\n                  </td>\n                </tr>\n              </tbody>\n            </table>\n          <p class=\"stem_paragraph \">The table above shows the amount of protein in two foods and the cost of each food. Based on the table, what is the ratio of the cost per gram of protein in a large egg to the cost per gram of protein in a cup of&nbsp;milk?</p></div>\n","answer":{"style":"Multiple Choice","choices":{"a":{"body":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \">1 : 2</p>\n"},"b":{"body":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \">2 : 3</p>\n"},"c":{"body":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \">3 : 4</p>\n"},"d":{"body":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \">2 : 1</p>\n"}},"correct_choice":"d","rationale":"<p>Choice D is correct. The cost per gram of protein in 1 large egg is $0.36 &divide; 6 = $0.06. The cost per gram of protein in 1 cup of milk is $0.24 &divide; 8 = $0.03. It follows that the ratio of the cost per gram of protein in a large egg to the cost per gram of protein in a cup of milk is&nbsp;0.06:0.03, which can be rewritten as 2:1.<p>Choice A is incorrect and may result from finding the ratio of the cost per gram of protein in a cup of milk to the cost per gram of protein in a large egg (the reciprocal of the ratio specified in the question). Choices B and C are incorrect and may result from incorrectly calculating the unit rates or from errors made when simplifying the ratio.</p></p>\n"}},"createDate":1691007959639,"updateDate":1691007959639}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1691007959639, 1691007959639),
    ($SATQ$7ed0d098$SATQ$, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$10596-DC$SATQ$, $SATQ$disclosed$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 2, $SATQ$Math$SATQ$, $SATQ$Problem-Solving and Data Analysis$SATQ$, $SATQ$Q$SATQ$, $SATQ$Q.B.$SATQ$, $SATQ$Percentages$SATQ$, $SATQ$E$SATQ$, 3, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, NULL, $SATQ$<p class="stem_paragraph ">Lani spent 15% of her 8-hour workday in meetings. How many <u><span class="underline"><span class="underline ">minutes</span></span></u> of her workday did she spend in meetings?</p>
$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"a","content":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \"><span class=\"align align-16\">1</span>.2</p>\n"},{"id":"b","content":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \"><span class=\"align align-16\">15</span></p>\n"},{"id":"c","content":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \"><span class=\"align align-16\">48</span></p>\n"},{"id":"d","content":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \"><span class=\"align align-16\">72</span></p>\n"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["D"]$SATQ$::jsonb, NULL, $SATQ$<p>Choice D is correct. There are 60 minutes in one hour, so an 8-hour workday has <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/7ed0d098/img_000_b973f9c3.png" alt="60 times 8, equals 480"></span> minutes. To calculate 15% of 480, multiply 0.15 by 480: <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/7ed0d098/img_001_23f199f9.png" alt="0 point 1 5 times 480, equals 72"></span>. Therefore, Lani spent 72 minutes of her workday in meetings.<p>Choice A is incorrect because 1.2 is 15% of 8, which gives the time Lani spent of her workday in meetings in hours, not minutes. Choices B and C are incorrect and may be the result of computation errors.</p><p>&nbsp;</p></p>
$SATQ$, false, 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$Multiple Choice$SATQ$, $SATQ$Math$SATQ$, $SATQ${"questionId":"7ed0d098","external_id":null,"disclosed_item_id":"10596-DC","source":"disclosed","program":"SAT","test_type":2,"test_type_desc":"Math","primary_class_cd":"Q","domain":"Problem-Solving and Data Analysis","skill_cd":"Q.B.","skill_desc":"Percentages","difficulty":"E","score_band_range_cd":3,"type":"mcq","stimulus":null,"stem":"<p class=\"stem_paragraph \">Lani spent 15% of her 8-hour workday in meetings. How many <u><span class=\"underline\"><span class=\"underline \">minutes</span></span></u> of her workday did she spend in meetings?</p>\n","answerOptions":[{"id":"a","content":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \"><span class=\"align align-16\">1</span>.2</p>\n"},{"id":"b","content":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \"><span class=\"align align-16\">15</span></p>\n"},{"id":"c","content":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \"><span class=\"align align-16\">48</span></p>\n"},{"id":"d","content":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \"><span class=\"align align-16\">72</span></p>\n"}],"keys":null,"correct_answer":["D"],"rationale":"<p>Choice D is correct. There are 60 minutes in one hour, so an 8-hour workday has <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/7ed0d098/img_000_b973f9c3.png\" alt=\"60 times 8, equals 480\"></span> minutes. To calculate 15% of 480, multiply 0.15 by 480: <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/7ed0d098/img_001_23f199f9.png\" alt=\"0 point 1 5 times 480, equals 72\"></span>. Therefore, Lani spent 72 minutes of her workday in meetings.<p>Choice A is incorrect because 1.2 is 15% of 8, which gives the time Lani spent of her workday in meetings in hours, not minutes. Choices B and C are incorrect and may be the result of computation errors.</p><p>&nbsp;</p></p>\n","answer_style":"Multiple Choice","section":"Math","image_count":2,"raw_list":{"updateDate":1691007959638,"pPcc":"SAT#Q","questionId":"7ed0d098","skill_cd":"Q.B.","score_band_range_cd":3,"skill_desc":"Percentages","createDate":1691007959638,"program":"SAT","primary_class_cd_desc":"Problem-Solving and Data Analysis","ibn":"10596-DC","external_id":null,"primary_class_cd":"Q","uId":"ab004bd2-8ca4-45e4-88f1-1d64fa5d5832","difficulty":"E"},"raw_detail":{"item_id":"10596-DC","section":"Math","prompt":"<p class=\"stem_paragraph \">Lani spent 15% of her 8-hour workday in meetings. How many <u><span class=\"underline\"><span class=\"underline \">minutes</span></span></u> of her workday did she spend in meetings?</p>\n","answer":{"style":"Multiple Choice","choices":{"a":{"body":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \"><span class=\"align align-16\">1</span>.2</p>\n"},"b":{"body":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \"><span class=\"align align-16\">15</span></p>\n"},"c":{"body":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \"><span class=\"align align-16\">48</span></p>\n"},"d":{"body":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \"><span class=\"align align-16\">72</span></p>\n"}},"correct_choice":"d","rationale":"<p>Choice D is correct. There are 60 minutes in one hour, so an 8-hour workday has <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"60 times 8, equals 480\"></span> minutes. To calculate 15% of 480, multiply 0.15 by 480: <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"0 point 1 5 times 480, equals 72\"></span>. Therefore, Lani spent 72 minutes of her workday in meetings.<p>Choice A is incorrect because 1.2 is 15% of 8, which gives the time Lani spent of her workday in meetings in hours, not minutes. Choices B and C are incorrect and may be the result of computation errors.</p><p>&nbsp;</p></p>\n"}},"createDate":1691007959638,"updateDate":1691007959638}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1691007959638, 1691007959638),
