/td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 22.3958px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 47.6772%; height: 22.3958px; text-align: center;\">Total</td>\n<td style=\"width: 47.6772%; height: 22.3958px; text-align: center;\"><math alttext=\"1,200\"><mn>1,200</mn>\n</math></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></figure>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The number of objects in group C is <math alttext=\"p percent sign\"><mi>p</mi><mo>%</mo></math> of the number of objects in group A. What is the value of <math alttext=\"p\"><mi>p</mi>\n</math>?</p>","keys":["184"],"rationale":"<p>The correct answer is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"184\"><mn>184</mn></math>. It's given in the table that there are <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"375\"><mn>375</mn></math> objects in group A and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"690\"><mn>690</mn></math> objects in group C. It&rsquo;s also given that the number of objects in group C is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"p percent sign\"><mi>p</mi><mo>%</mo></math> of the number of objects in group A. Therefore, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"690\"><mn>690</mn></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"p percent sign\"><mi>p</mi><mo>%</mo></math> of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"375\"><mn>375</mn></math>, which can be represented by&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"690 equals left parenthesis StartFraction p Over 100 EndFraction right parenthesis left parenthesis 375 right parenthesis\"><mn>690</mn><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mfrac><mi>p</mi><mn>100</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mfenced><mn>375</mn></mfenced></math>, or <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"690 equals 3.75 p\"><mn>690</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>3.75</mn><mi>p</mi></math>. Dividing both sides of this equation by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"3.75\"><mn>3.75</mn></math>&nbsp;yields <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"184 equals p\"><mn>184</mn><mo>=</mo><mi>p</mi></math>. Therefore, the value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"p\"><mi>p</mi></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"184\"><mn>184</mn></math>.</p>","externalid":"b3f57376-4374-4b2d-ab34-98d991fed767","correct_answer":["184"]},"createDate":1755117017722,"updateDate":1755117017722}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1755117017722, 1755117017722),
    ($SATQ$7fd284ac$SATQ$, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$08424-DC$SATQ$, $SATQ$disclosed$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 2, $SATQ$Math$SATQ$, $SATQ$Problem-Solving and Data Analysis$SATQ$, $SATQ$Q$SATQ$, $SATQ$Q.D.$SATQ$, $SATQ$Two-variable data: Models and scatterplots$SATQ$, $SATQ$M$SATQ$, 5, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, $SATQ$<div class="stimulus_reference " xmlns="http://www.imsglobal.org/xsd/apip/apipv1p0/qtiitem/imsqti_v2p1"><div class="standalone_image "><img src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/7fd284ac/img_004_23f4c191.png" alt="The figure presents a scatterplot titled &ldquo;Income and Percent of Total Expenses Spent on Programs for Ten Charities in 2011.&rdquo; The horizontal axis is labeled &ldquo;Total income,&rdquo; in millions of dollars, and the numbers zero through 7,000, in increments of 1,000, are indicated. The vertical axis is labeled &ldquo;Percent of total expenses spent on programs&rdquo; and the numbers 70 through 95, in increments of 5, are indicated. 

