,168.393c0-1.757.381-3.236,1.143-4.438s1.79-1.802,3.082-1.802c1.305,0,2.335.598,3.091,1.792.755,1.195,1.133,2.678,1.133,4.448,0,1.757-.381,3.236-1.143,4.438-.763,1.202-1.79,1.802-3.082,1.802-1.279,0-2.303-.604-3.072-1.812s-1.153-2.684-1.153-4.428Zm1.705-.02c0,1.55.226,2.858.678,3.924s1.034,1.599,1.745,1.599c.827,0,1.469-.536,1.928-1.608.458-1.072.688-2.41.688-4.012,0-1.538-.227-2.82-.678-3.847-.453-1.027-1.034-1.541-1.745-1.541-.788,0-1.421.523-1.899,1.57-.478,1.046-.717,2.352-.717,3.915Z\" stroke-width=\"0\"></path><path d=\"m39.673,191.451c0-1.757.381-3.236,1.143-4.438s1.79-1.802,3.082-1.802c1.305,0,2.335.598,3.091,1.792.755,1.195,1.133,2.678,1.133,4.448,0,1.757-.381,3.236-1.143,4.438-.763,1.202-1.79,1.802-3.082,1.802-1.279,0-2.303-.604-3.072-1.812s-1.153-2.684-1.153-4.428Zm1.705-.02c0,1.55.226,2.858.678,3.924s1.034,1.599,1.745,1.599c.827,0,1.469-.536,1.928-1.608.458-1.072.688-2.41.688-4.012,0-1.538-.227-2.82-.678-3.847-.453-1.027-1.034-1.541-1.745-1.541-.788,0-1.421.523-1.899,1.57-.478,1.046-.717,2.352-.717,3.915Z\" stroke-width=\"0\"></path></svg><div role=\"region\" aria-label=\"Long description for bar graph\" class=\"sr-only\"><ul>\n<li>The Frequency data for the 4 bars are as follows:<br>\n<ul>\n<li>blue: 27</li>\n<li>green: 70</li>\n<li>red: 33</li>\n<li>yellow: 43</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul></div></figure></p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">&nbsp;</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">A data set consists of <math alttext=\"173\"><mn>173</mn>\n</math> colors. The bar graph shows the number of times each color appears in the data set. Which color appears <math alttext=\"70\"><mn>70</mn>\n</math> times?</p>","keys":["6ba1befb-15d3-42a9-adb7-43c1268463b6"],"answerOptions":[{"id":"02487fab-e148-407d-8da4-ed1ca6143d33","content":"<p>Blue</p>"},{"id":"6ba1befb-15d3-42a9-adb7-43c1268463b6","content":"<p>Green</p>"},{"id":"7d3e439e-7a12-4f0f-ba8a-90830f4c151b","content":"<p>Red</p>"},{"id":"76b02997-fdb8-431f-a2ea-903abd94fc1c","content":"<p>Yellow</p>"}],"rationale":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice B is correct. It's given that a data set consists of <math alttext=\"173\"><mn>173</mn>\n</math> colors and the bar graph shows the number of times each color appears in the data set. Therefore, for each color specified at the bottom of the bar, the frequency corresponds to the number of times that color appears in the data set. The color that appears <math alttext=\"70\"><mn>70</mn>\n</math> times in the data set has a frequency of <math alttext=\"70\"><mn>70</mn>\n</math> on the bar graph. Since the bar with a frequency of <math alttext=\"70\"><mn>70</mn>\n</math> corresponds to green, green is the color that appears <math alttext=\"70\"><mn>70</mn>\n</math> times.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice A is incorrect. The color blue appears about <math alttext=\"27\"><mn>27</mn>\n</math> times, not <math alttext=\"70\"><mn>70</mn>\n</math> times.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice C is incorrect. The color red appears about <math alttext=\"33\"><mn>33</mn>\n</math> times, not <math alttext=\"70\"><mn>70</mn>\n</math> times.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice D is incorrect. The color yellow appears about <math alttext=\"43\"><mn>43</mn>\n</math> times, not <math alttext=\"70\"><mn>70</mn>\n</math> times.</p>","externalid":"1010b663-23d7-48e5-8a54-02a9c7c6a552","correct_answer":["B"]},"createDate":1743430554980,"updateDate":1743430554980}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1743430554980, 1743430554980),
    ($SATQ$8156d446$SATQ$, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$070917-DC$SATQ$, $SATQ$disclosed$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 2, $SATQ$Math$SATQ$, $SATQ$Problem-Solving and Data Analysis$SATQ$, $SATQ$Q$SATQ$, $SATQ$Q.D.$SATQ$, $SATQ$Two-variable data: Models and scatterplots$SATQ$, $SATQ$E$SATQ$, 3, $SATQ$spr$SATQ$, NULL, $SATQ$<p><img src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/8156d446/img_000_7861ddb2.png" alt="The figure presents a scatterplot titled &ldquo;Number of Beach Visitors versus Temperature.&rdquo; The horizontal axis is labeled &ldquo;Average temperature, in degrees Celsius,&rdquo; and the numbers 25 through 35, in increments of 2, are indicated. The vertical axis is labeled &ldquo;Number of people,&rdquo; and the numbers 0 through 640, in increments of 80, are indicated. There are 11 data points in the scatterplot that begin near the bottom left portion of the coordinate plane and trend upward and to the right. The line of best fit for the data is also shown. The line of best fit passes through the points with coordinates 25 comma 80 and 32 comma 480." width="187" height="205">
        <p class="stem_paragraph ">Each dot in the scatterplot above represents the temperature and the number of people who visited a beach in Lagos, Nigeria, on one of eleven different days. The line of best fit for the data is also shown. According to the line of best fit, what is the number of people, rounded to the nearest 10, predicted to visit this beach on a day with an average temperature of 32&deg;C?</p></p>
$SATQ$, NULL, $SATQ$["480"]$SATQ$::jsonb, NULL, $SATQ$<p>The correct answer is 480. An average temperature of <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/8156d446/img_001_9009ba8c.png" alt="32 degrees Celsius"></span> corresponds to the value 32 on the <span class="italic">x</span>-axis. On the line of best fit, an <span class="italic">x</span>-value of 32 corresponds to a <span class="italic">y</span>-value of 480. The values on the <span class="italic">y</span>-axis correspond to the number of people predicted to visit this beach. Therefore, 480 people are predicted to visit this beach on a day with an average temperature of <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/8156d446/img_002_9009ba8c.png" alt="32 degrees Celsius"></span>.</p>
$SATQ$, true, 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$SPR$SATQ$, $SATQ$Math$SATQ$, $SATQ${"questionId":"8156d446","external_id":null,"disclosed_item_id":"070917-DC","source":"disclosed","program":"SAT","test_type":2,"test_type_desc":"Math","primary_class_cd":"Q","domain":"Problem-Solving and Data Analysis","skill_cd":"Q.D.","skill_desc":"Two-variable data: Models and scatterplots","difficulty":"E","score_band_range_cd":3,"type":"spr","stimulus":null,"stem":"<p><img src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/8156d446/img_000_7861ddb2.png\" alt=\"The figure presents a scatterplot titled &ldquo;Number of Beach Visitors versus Temperature.&rdquo; The horizontal axis is labeled &ldquo;Average temperature, in degrees Celsius,&rdquo; and the numbers 25 through 35, in increments of 2, are indicated. The vertical axis is labeled &ldquo;Number of people,&rdquo; and the numbers 0 through 640, in increments of 80, are indicated. There are 11 data points in the scatterplot that begin near the bottom left portion of the coordinate plane and trend upward and to the right. The line of best fit for the data is also shown. The line of best fit passes through the points with coordinates 25 comma 80 and 32 comma 480.\" width=\"187\" height=\"205\">\n        <p class=\"stem_paragraph \">Each dot in the scatterplot above represents the temperature and the number of people who visited a beach in Lagos, Nigeria, on one of eleven different days. The line of best fit for the data is also shown. According to the line of best fit, what is the number of people, rounded to the nearest 10, predicted to visit this beach on a day with an average temperature of 32&deg;C?</p></p>\n","answerOptions":null,"keys":null,"correct_answer":["480"],"rationale":"<p>The correct answer is 480. An average temperature of <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/8156d446/img_001_9009ba8c.png\" alt=\"32 degrees Celsius\"></span> corresponds to the value 32 on the <span class=\"italic\">x</span>-axis. On the line of best fit, an <span class=\"italic\">x</span>-value of 32 corresponds to a <span class=\"italic\">y</span>-value of 480. The values on the <span class=\"italic\">y</span>-axis correspond to the number of people predicted to visit this beach. Therefore, 480 people are predicted to visit this beach on a day with an average temperature of <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/8156d446/img_002_9009ba8c.png\" alt=\"32 degrees Celsius\"></span>.</p>\n","answer_style":"SPR","section":"Math","image_count":3,"raw_list":{"updateDate":1691007959633,"pPcc":"SAT#Q","questionId":"8156d446","skill_cd":"Q.D.","score_band_range_cd":3,"skill_desc":"Two-variable data: Models and scatterplots","createDate":1691007959633,"program":"SAT","primary_class_cd_desc":"Problem-Solving and Data Analysis","ibn":"070917-DC","external_id":null,"primary_class_cd":"Q","uId":"c1c10651-e7cd-4ef5-a45c-9af28c730d3d","difficulty":"E"},"raw_detail":{"item_id":"070917-DC","section":"Math","prompt":"<p><img src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"The figure presents a scatterplot titled &ldquo;Number of Beach Visitors versus Temperature.&rdquo; The horizontal axis is labeled &ldquo;Average temperature, in degrees Celsius,&rdquo; and the numbers 25 through 35, in increments of 2, are indicated. The vertical axis is labeled &ldquo;Number of people,&rdquo; and the numbers 0 through 640, in increments of 80, are indicated. There are 11 data points in the scatterplot that begin near the bottom left portion of the coordinate plane and trend upward and to the right. The line of best fit for the data is also shown. The line of best fit passes through the points with coordinates 25 comma 80 and 32 comma 480.\" width=\"187\" height=\"205\">\n        <p class=\"stem_paragraph \">Each dot in the scatterplot above represents the temperature and the number of people who visited a beach in Lagos, Nigeria, on one of eleven different days. The line of best fit for the data is also shown. According to the line of best fit, what is the number of people, rounded to the nearest 10, predicted to visit this beach on a day with an average temperature of 32&deg;C?</p></p>\n","answer":{"style":"SPR","rationale":"<p>The correct answer is 480. An average temperature of <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"32 degrees Celsius\"></span> corresponds to the value 32 on the <span class=\"italic\">x</span>-axis. On the line of best fit, an <span class=\"italic\">x</span>-value of 32 corresponds to a <span class=\"italic\">y</span>-value of 480. The values on the <span class=\"italic\">y</span>-axis correspond to the number of people predicted to visit this beach. Therefore, 480 people are predicted to visit this beach on a day with an average temperature of <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"32 degrees Celsius\"></span>.</p>\n"}},"createDate":1691007959633,"updateDate":1691007959633,"correct_answer_extracted_from_rationale":true}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1691007959633, 1691007959633),
    ($SATQ$8173f32b$SATQ$, $SATQ$c2be4ad8-5127-48a8-8cd4-4a6d2c61e2c6$SATQ$::uuid, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$qbank$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 2, $SATQ$Math$SATQ$, $SATQ$Problem-Solving and Data Analysis$SATQ$, $SATQ$Q$SATQ$, $SATQ$Q.F.$SATQ$, $SATQ$Inference from sample statistics and margin of error $SATQ$, $SATQ$E$SATQ$, 2, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, NULL, $SATQ$<p style="text-align: left;">An analyst collected data on the price of a carton of grape tomatoes at <math alttext="30"><mn>30</mn>
</math> locations selected at random in Utah. The mean price of a carton of grape tomatoes in Utah was estimated to be <math alttext="dollar sign 4.23"><mo>$</mo><mn>4.23</mn></math>, with an associated margin of error of <math alttext="dollar sign 0.08"><mo>$</mo><mn>0.08</mn></math>. Which of the following is a plausible statement about the mean price of a carton of grape tomatoes for all locations that sell this product in Utah?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"53bcf8de-802b-4d3c-94da-c4039ec6f72f","content":"<p>It is between <math alttext=\"dollar sign 4.15\"><mo>$</mo><mn>4.15</mn></math> and <math alttext=\"dollar sign 4.31\"><mo>$</mo><mn>4.31</mn></math>.</p>"},{"id":"35c73b6d-c388-4d3d-9068-f262f19a5131","content":"<p>It is either less than <math alttext=\"dollar sign 4.15\"><mo>$</mo><mn>4.15</mn></math> or greater than <math alttext=\"dollar sign 4.31\"><mo>$</mo><mn>4.31</mn></math>.</p>"},{"id":"1ffadcf3-1e54-4c25-a1fb-786fb83fe449","content":"<p>It is less than <math alttext=\"dollar sign 4.15\"><mo>$</mo><mn>4.15</mn></math>.</p>"},{"id":"add38af9-ef0b-4b3b-82f9-62bf9472bb21","content":"<p>It is greater than <math alttext=\"dollar sign 4.31\"><mo>$</mo><mn>4.31</mn></math>.</p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["A"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["53bcf8de-802b-4d3c-94da-c4039ec6f72f"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p style="text-align: left;">Choice A is correct. It's given that the mean price of a carton of grape tomatoes in Utah was estimated to be <math alttext="dollar sign 4.23"><mo>$</mo><mn>4.23</mn></math>, with an associated margin of error of&nbsp;<math alttext="dollar sign 0.08"><mo>$</mo><mn>0.08</mn></math>. It follows that plausible values for this mean price are between <math alttext="dollar sign 4.23 minus dollar sign 0.08"><mo>$</mo><mn>4.23</mn><mo>-</mo><mo>$</mo><mn>0.08</mn></math> and&nbsp;<math alttext="dollar sign 4.23 plus dollar sign 0.08"><mo>$</mo><mn>4.23</mn><mo>+</mo><mo>$</mo><mn>0.08</mn></math>. Therefore, it's plausible that the mean price of a carton of grape tomatoes for all locations that sell this product in Utah is between <math alttext="dollar sign 4.15"><mo>$</mo><mn>4.15</mn></math> and&nbsp;<math alttext="dollar sign 4.31"><mo>$</mo><mn>4.31</mn></math>.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice B is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice C is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>
