$SATQ$, NULL, $SATQ$["1/5",".2"]$SATQ$::jsonb, NULL, $SATQ$<p>The correct answer is <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/8193e8cd/img_001_5dba61cf.png" alt="one fifth"></span>. The mean of the list of numbers is found by dividing the sum of the numbers by the number of values in the list. Since there are 5 numbers in the list, the mean is <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/8193e8cd/img_002_5dba61cf.png" alt="one fifth"></span> of the sum of the numbers. Note that 1/5 and .2 are examples of ways to enter a correct answer.</p>
