</math> grams, what is the maximum mass, in grams, of phosphorus the sample can contain to meet these standards?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$[".0014"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$[".0014"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p style="text-align: left;">The correct answer is <math alttext=".0014"><mo>.0014</mo></math>. It's given that a certain type of substance can contain a maximum of <math alttext="0.001 percent sign"><mn>0.001</mn><mo>%</mo></math> phosphorus by mass to meet a set of standards. If a sample of the substance has a mass of <math alttext="140"><mn>140</mn>
